# Durable project design memory (spec 27) is committed on purpose:
# it is meant to be read, diffed and corrected by a human.

# Design snapshots are per-user checkpoints with full programs in them.
# They would bloat the repo and go stale; memory (above) is the shared part.
.snapshots/

# Job-ledger restart persistence (opt-in via DESIGN_AGENT_JOB_DIR)
.jobs/

# Cross-run repair trace (runtime log, recreated at runtime; never commit test rows)
artifacts/repair-history.jsonl

